aquinas-first-way.logic.r2: argue/scope: P2 (S3): read with the necessity on its consequent alone, motion_is_reduction ∧ reduction_needs_actual → □(self_moves → act_pot_same), the argument holds; read with it on the whole conditional, □(motion_is_reduction ∧ reduction_needs_actual → (self_moves → act_pot_same)), C1 (S9) does not follow: it needs the necessity of the consequent, not only of the consequence, and which the sentence means decides the argument
